#!/usr/bin/python3
"""kioskd -- the root-side half of the kiosk.

Serves the Settings/Installer page (/usr/share/immutable-kiosk/web) and a small
JSON API on 127.0.0.1:8088 for everything that needs root: Wi-Fi and IP
(nmcli), the HMI address, system updates (bootc) and, on the installer ISO,
writing the system onto the internal disk.

Only kiosk-shell's Settings view is meant to talk to it. Two guards keep any
other page (the HMI included) out:
  * every /api request must carry "X-Kiosk: 1" -- a custom header a foreign
    origin can't send without a CORS preflight, which is never answered;
  * the Host header must be 127.0.0.1:8088 / localhost:8088 (DNS rebinding).

Python stdlib only, so nothing extra lands in the image.
"""

